==Significance==
Taken together, the measured dilepton mass spectra, transverse-momentum distributions, and angular distributions provide a largely model-independent signature of thermal radiation from the hot and dense medium created in heavy-ion collisions and establish thermal dileptons as an experimental thermometer for quark–gluon matter.<ref>{{cite book
